{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"125a789d3eb17e24","name":"card_event_stealth_mission","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_stealth_mission","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"STEALTH MISSION","text":"Give a friendly unit: \"Remove from the battlefield at the start of your turn to gain 6 kredits and draw 3 cards.\"","flavorText":"Five Japanese submarines, known as the \"midget submarines\", were part of the attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941. Their objective was to penetrate the harbor defenses and launch torpedoes at American ships. These submarines were relatively small, crewed by only two or three men, and carried two torpedoes each. The midget submarines encountered various challenges during their mission. One of them, Ha-19, became entangled in an anti-submarine net and was eventually scuttled by its crew, and submarine Ha-20, was sunk by the USS Helm. While the midget submarines did not cause significant damage to American warships, their presence added to the chaos and confusion during the attack. Their role in the attack highlights the Japanese Navy's strategy of employing various naval assets, including submarines, to maximize the impact of their operations. It is worth noting that Japanese submarines conducted numerous other missions throughout WWII, including patrols, reconnaissance, and attacks on enemy ships. However, the attack on Pearl Harbor remains one of the most notable examples of Japanese submarine operations during the war.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_stealth_mission","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_stealth_mission_title","SourceString":"STEALTH MISSION","LocalizedString":"STEALTH MISSION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_stealth_mission_text","SourceString":"Give a friendly unit: \"Remove from the battlefield at the start of your turn to gain 6 kredits and draw 3 cards.\"","LocalizedString":"Give a friendly unit: \"Remove from the battlefield at the start of your turn to gain 6 kredits and draw 3 cards.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_stealth_mission_history","SourceString":"Five Japanese submarines, known as the \"midget submarines\", were part of the attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941. Their objective was to penetrate the harbor defenses and launch torpedoes at American ships. These submarines were relatively small, crewed by only two or three men, and carried two torpedoes each. The midget submarines encountered various challenges during their mission. One of them, Ha-19, became entangled in an anti-submarine net and was eventually scuttled by its crew, and submarine Ha-20, was sunk by the USS Helm. While the midget submarines did not cause significant damage to American warships, their presence added to the chaos and confusion during the attack. Their role in the attack highlights the Japanese Navy's strategy of employing various naval assets, including submarines, to maximize the impact of their operations. It is worth noting that Japanese submarines conducted numerous other missions throughout WWII, including patrols, reconnaissance, and attacks on enemy ships. However, the attack on Pearl Harbor remains one of the most notable examples of Japanese submarine operations during the war.","LocalizedString":"Five Japanese submarines, known as the \"midget submarines\", were part of the attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941. Their objective was to penetrate the harbor defenses and launch torpedoes at American ships. These submarines were relatively small, crewed by only two or three men, and carried two torpedoes each. The midget submarines encountered various challenges during their mission. One of them, Ha-19, became entangled in an anti-submarine net and was eventually scuttled by its crew, and submarine Ha-20, was sunk by the USS Helm. While the midget submarines did not cause significant damage to American warships, their presence added to the chaos and confusion during the attack. Their role in the attack highlights the Japanese Navy's strategy of employing various naval assets, including submarines, to maximize the impact of their operations. It is worth noting that Japanese submarines conducted numerous other missions throughout WWII, including patrols, reconnaissance, and attacks on enemy ships. However, the attack on Pearl Harbor remains one of the most notable examples of Japanese submarine operations during the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Spring2023Candidates/t_stealth_mission.t_stealth_mission","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/STEALTH_MISSION.STEALTH_MISSION","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":353.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_stealth_mission_photo","SourceString":"A Nishimura-style Japanese midget submarine, ca. 1940.","LocalizedString":"A Nishimura-style Japanese midget submarine, ca. 1940."},"isDraw":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tmpCardID","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"found","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"affectedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_stealth_mission_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"